Title: cJSON_AddObjectToObject with a cJSON* parameter?
Description: Is there any possibility to add a cJSON* object to another cJSON* object? The function that sounds like it would do what I want takes a string as parameter and doesn't seem to have any alternatives. Let me show why I need it:
I have two structs:

```c
typedef struct pet_t {
category_t *category;
} pet_t;
typedef struct category_t {
char *name;
long id;
} category_t;
```
Now I would like to have a method for both of them like that:
```c
cJSON* pet_toJSON(pet_t *pet);
cJSON* category_toJSON(category_t *category);
```
The implementation I would like to have like that:
```c
cJSON *pet_toJSON(pet_t *pet) {
cJSON *petJSONObject = cJSON_CreateObject();
cJSON *categoryJSONObject = category_toJSON(pet->category);
cJSON_AddObjectToObject(petJSONObject, "category", categoryJSONObject);
```
Currently this is not possible and I do it like that:
```c
cJSON *pet_toJSON(pet_t *pet) {
cJSON *petJSONObject = cJSON_CreateObject();
cJSON *categoryJSONObject;
if(cJSON_AddObjectToObject(petJSONObject, "category") == NULL) {
	goto end;
}
categoryJSONObject = cJSON_GetObjectItem(petJSONObject,
	                                                "category");
if(cJSON_AddNumberToObject(categoryJSONObject, "id",
	                           pet->category->id) == NULL)
{
	goto end;
}
// Category->name
if(cJSON_AddStringToObject(categoryJSONObject, "name",
	                          pet->category->name) == NULL)
{
	goto end;
}
```

Is there any way to add a already created JSON Object to another one?

